   "titulo": "Verbs with være",
   "texto": [
    "**Have** is the most widespread auxiliary; **være** appears with certain intransitive verbs of movement or state change: **Hun er kommet hjem.** = It has arrived home. The choice may also depend on the meaning: **Hun er cyklet hjem** (has been on a bike home), but **Hun har cyklet hele dagen** (has been pedaling all day). Learn the frequent uses with each verb and context."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Remaining verbs",
   "texto": [
    "With the rest of the verbs use **have**: **Han har løbet hele vejen.** = It has run all the way. **Vi har læst bogen.** = We have read the book.",
    "Compare: **Han er løbet hjem.** (has come running home) and **Han har løbet hele vejen.** (has run all the way)."
